title start
kind: research
tags: business-plan legal-and-finance legal-finance-disclosure-rules-by-platform
Legal finance disclosure rules by platform
title end

section start
title start
Abstract
title end

paragraph start
Question: when and how must paid, gifted and affiliate content be disclosed. Method: a web search of legal and trade commentary on the United States Endorsement Guides, read on 2026-10-29. Result: sources agree that any material connection, including affiliate links and free products, must be disclosed clearly and conspicuously, near the claim, in plain language. Limit: all sources are secondary, only United States rules were searched, and the primary rule text was not read.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Introduction
title end

paragraph start
The brand plans donations, affiliate links, shop links and sponsorships from the first day, so disclosure rules apply from the first post. This page records the evidence found and what is still unverified.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Methods
title end

paragraph start
Searched the web for commentary on the Federal Trade Commission Endorsement Guides, codified in a rule part numbered 255 in title 16 of the federal regulations, and read several law firm and trade articles. The official text was not opened.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Results
title end

paragraph start
Secondary sources say a material connection is any link between endorser and advertiser that could affect how the audience weighs the endorsement, and that it covers payment, free products and commission on affiliate links (track360 and others, checked 2026-10-29).
paragraph end

paragraph start
Secondary sources say a disclosure must be hard to miss and easy to understand for ordinary consumers, and that a platform built in tool may not be enough on its own (Marketing Dive, secondary).
paragraph end

paragraph start
Secondary sources report that the agency advised placing the disclosure before the more button on Instagram captions and avoiding burying it among many hashtags or links (Fashion Law, secondary).
paragraph end

paragraph start
Secondary sources say the 2023 update extended the guides to tags, virtual endorsers and fake reviews (Arnold and Porter, secondary).
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Discussion
title end

paragraph start
Working rule for the plan until verified: disclose every paid, gifted or affiliate relationship in the caption start and in the video itself, in plain words, before the viewer must click anything. Law differs by country, and the owner country is not yet chosen.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: read the official rule text and the agency guidance, then confirm the working rule and the rules of the owner country
Not verified yet.
paragraph end

section end

